1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,160
It's six forty-five

2
00:00:01,170 --> 00:00:01,950
in the morning.

3
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:03,570
Marco just called in sick.

4
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:04,650
Four customers are waiting

5
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:05,640
for him today.

6
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:07,120
Who covers his jobs?

7
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:07,850
Figuring that out

8
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:09,330
by hand takes an hour.

9
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:10,180
Second Shift does it

10
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:11,210
in seconds.

11
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:19,310
Someone posts in Slack:

12
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:20,430
Marco is out.

13
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:21,560
Second Shift reads it,

14
00:00:21,570 --> 00:00:22,630
then looks at every job

15
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:23,850
and every calendar.

16
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,580
It builds a new plan.

17
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:31,030
Watch the trucks move.

18
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:31,900
Wei can do Marco's

19
00:00:31,910 --> 00:00:32,620
big gas job,

20
00:00:32,630 --> 00:00:33,790
but he's busy.

21
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,450
So Ana takes

22
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:35,410
Wei's small job,

23
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:36,940
and Wei takes Marco's.

24
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:37,610
One job can't

25
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,490
be saved today,

26
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:39,520
so that customer is asked

27
00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:40,710
to pick a new time.

28
00:00:50,390 --> 00:00:51,430
Nothing changes until

29
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,910
a person says yes.

30
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:53,560
One click,

31
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:54,890
and it updates the calendars

32
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:55,800
and the job sheet,

33
00:00:55,810 --> 00:00:57,180
messages the team in Slack,

34
00:00:57,190 --> 00:00:58,780
and emails the customers.

35
00:01:05,598 --> 00:01:07,358
Then it double-checks every change.

36
00:01:07,368 --> 00:01:09,208
Thirty-six out of thirty-six.

37
00:01:09,218 --> 00:01:10,408
If it crashes halfway,

38
00:01:10,418 --> 00:01:10,918
it finishes

39
00:01:10,928 --> 00:01:12,738
without sending anything twice.

40
00:01:12,748 --> 00:01:13,548
And you can ask:

41
00:01:13,558 --> 00:01:14,018
what if Wei

42
00:01:14,028 --> 00:01:15,108
doesn't show up?

43
00:01:15,118 --> 00:01:15,708
It shows you,

44
00:01:15,718 --> 00:01:16,988
before it happens.

45
00:01:25,908 --> 00:01:26,508
Sick days,

46
00:01:26,518 --> 00:01:28,328
flat tires, no-shows.

47
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:29,648
They'll keep happening.

48
00:01:29,658 --> 00:01:30,558
Now they take seconds

49
00:01:30,568 --> 00:01:31,308
to fix,

50
00:01:31,318 --> 00:01:32,228
not an hour.

51
00:01:32,238 --> 00:01:33,468
We can't predict the day.

52
00:01:33,478 --> 00:01:34,248
But we can be ready

53
00:01:34,258 --> 00:01:35,028
for it.

54
00:01:35,038 --> 00:01:36,108
Second Shift.

